-- title:
--   Genus of quotients of the Drinfeld curve by μ_{q+1}-subgroups
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over the Galois field $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ (`GaloisField q 2`), and suppose the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,k$ by the ideal generated by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,k - 1$, is a domain. Let $C$ be a subgroup of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Write $DL = \mathrm{drinfeldFunctionField}\,q\,k$ for the fraction field of `CoordRing q k`, and let $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,k\,C$ be the intermediate field of $k \subseteq DL$ fixed by the subgroup of $k$-algebra automorphisms of $DL$ generated by the images under `hFunctionFieldAction` of the elements $(1,\zeta)$ of `hSubgroup q` for $\zeta$ running over $C$. With $g = \mathrm{genusFF}\,k\,(\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,k\,C)$, the $k$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor (divisors being finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on the places of this extension), and $n = |C|$, the assertion is the identity of natural numbers
--   $$n\,(2g + q) + 1 = q^2 + n,$$
--   equivalently $n\,(2g + q - 1) = q^2 - 1$.
--
--   This computes the genus of the quotient of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ by a group of $n$ scalars in $\mu_{q+1}$, in the uniform multiplicative shape $n(2g+q-1) = q^2-1$; for $n = 1$ it returns the genus $q(q-1)/2$ of the curve itself, and for $n = q+1$ it gives $g = 0$. It feeds the genus computations for the charts of the semistable covering of modular curves at full level, used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_placeWidthChar_mul_genusFF_add_of_chart_over`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_placeWidthChar_mul_genusFF_add_of_chart_over) and its variants for the primes $2$ and $3$.
